    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To implement the requested Python files for static image and visual understanding tasks using Google Cloud Vision API, I need to create the following files:\n\n1. detect_image_labels.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Vision API to detect labels or objects in a static image.\n2. describe_image.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Vision API to generate a short visual description for an image.\n3. detect_image_text.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Vision API to detect text appearing inside an image.\n4. score_image_safety.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Vision API to check an image for unsafe or policy-sensitive visual content.\n5. vision_client.py - This helper file will provide local configuration and client utilities for the Google Cloud Vision API.\n6. vision_models.py - This helper file will define local request, response, and normalization helpers for the Google Cloud Vision API.\n7. image_summary.py - This file will summarize visual analysis results.\n8. alt_text_translate.py - This file will translate generated image descriptions.\n9. visual_safety_text.py - This file will check generated visual labels for unsafe text.\n10. image_asset_archive.py - This file will archive image-analysis artifacts and derived captions in managed object storage.\n\nI will start by creating the vision_client.py and vision_models.py helper files, followed by the [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789842250071,
          "start": 1789842238763
        },
